  "preamble": "Voicing of the glottal fricative /h/ to breathy-voiced [ɦ] between voiced sounds, where the glottis keeps vibrating through the consonant. It is a common allophony: Finnish /h/ is murmured [ɦ] in voiced contexts (maha [ˈmɑɦɑ] 'belly'), Hungarian /h/ is [ɦ] between vowels (tehát [ˈtɛɦaːt]), and English /h/ in words such as behind and ahead is [ɦ] in RP and Australian English. The same intervocalic voicing of /h/ is described for Danish, Estonian and Modern Hebrew.",
